cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite the repository and the version you consulted."
type: software
title: "grAIph: A Graph-First Visual Environment for Bounded Agentic Development"
abstract: >
  grAIph is a research system for representing software architecture as explicit,
  shared graph state. The graph drives visualization, topological context
  compilation, bounded capability selection, candidate generation, validation,
  evidence reconciliation, and host-controlled commit. The public repository
  documents the architecture, hypotheses, benchmark protocol, bounded evidence,
  and current claim boundaries; the implementation remains private while the
  system is being hardened.
